# NIVO human-crafted UI

NIVO is for international students arriving in Germany. Interfaces should feel calm, specific, and hand-built — not like a default AI landing or dashboard kit.

## Brand & layout

- Keep NIVO orange (`#FB770B`), charcoal, paper/mist. Do not drift into purple gradients, glow stacks, or cream+terracotta “AI portfolio” looks.
- Brand-first on marketing: if removing the nav would still leave a clear NIVO identity, branding is strong enough.
- One job per section. Prefer hairline rules and uneven grids over identical card grids with soft shadows.
- Cards only when they wrap a real interaction. If border/shadow/radius can go without hurting understanding, remove them.
- Hero budget: brand, one headline, one support line, one CTA group, one dominant atmosphere — no stats strips, pill clusters, or floating badges on media.

## Copy (anti-AI voice)

- Speak to a student preparing for Germany: Sperrkonto, visa docs, housing, SIM — concrete, not “unlock your potential.”
- Prefer plain verbs: Start, Continue, Upload, Open. Avoid “Get started on your journey to excellence.”
- Do not accent a single random word in a headline with italic/color.
- Avoid ALL-CAPS eyebrows on every block. If a label is needed, use a short sentence-case line in orange-dark or soft charcoal.
- Partner/commission language stays honest and short (NIVO introduces; student contracts with the partner).

## Motion

- Animate for feedback, orientation, or one deliberate entrance — not decoration.
- **Landing:** at most one orchestrated load moment (e.g. hero). Do not `rise-in` / fade-up every section or list item (classic AI tell).
- **App chrome:** prefer CSS transitions on hover/active/open/close. High-frequency UI enters fast (≈0–100ms), exits briefly (100–150ms).
- Use `transform` + `opacity` only for movement. Never `transition: all`. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (already in `index.css`).
- Confirm in place when possible (button label → “Saved”) before relying on corner toasts.
- Press feedback: `:active { transform: scale(0.98) }` at 0ms on tappable controls.

## LandingFolio / external inspiration

- Free LandingFolio ≈ **20 calls/day** — check agent-store `landingfolio-usage.md` before calling; prefer ≤2 calls per design pass.
- LandingFolio returns **static screenshots**, not live animation or code. Tag `animation` only finds pages that look motion-heavy in a still.
- Always **adapt** into NIVO tokens; never 1:1 clone a SaaS screenshot’s colors/type unless the user asks.
- Live motion and previews: implement in-app (CSS / existing patterns); use browser preview or Playwright — not LandingFolio.

## Quick “AI tell” checklist (reject if present)

- Staggered fade/slide-up on every block
- Tracked ALL-CAPS labels above every heading
- Three identical rounded cards with the same shadow
- Purple/indigo gradient theme or glassmorphism stack
- Generic stock metaphor with no Germany/student specificity
- Mid-dot meta rows (`A · B · C`) as decoration
